                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2100885e-a8dd-3207-aaba-5feee921b7e8",
                        "entry_id": "5529d329-b541-39d0-876e-ee1f0a77cedc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Segment terminal postérieur du corps des arthropodes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "36a8fd75-e124-4627-9f7a-5da89693cb15",
                                "sense_id": "2100885e-a8dd-3207-aaba-5feee921b7e8",
                                "text": "...un soma segmenté (le corps proprement dit) et un telson non segmenté, très réduit, ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69f0e6b3-7f4f-44dc-9197-f00fef6d92a0",
                                "sense_id": "2100885e-a8dd-3207-aaba-5feee921b7e8",
                                "text": "Ce vaisseau peut, à bon droit, être ajouté à la catégorie des vaisseaux branchio-péricardiques, car le telson joue le rôle de branchie, et cette fonction explique pourquoi nous avons réservé un article spécial à la circulation dans ce segment."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3d5e8d30-529f-4204-9c59-29f1f43229be",
                        "source_entry_id": "5529d329-b541-39d0-876e-ee1f0a77cedc",
                        "source_sense_id": "2100885e-a8dd-3207-aaba-5feee921b7e8",
                        "target_lang_word": "telson",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "telson",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "273898fe-fc06-3d46-9c54-6911e31df727",
                                        "entry_id": "bc66849c-b17a-3330-b46e-9b6d5e615938",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The part of an arthropod or crustacean posterior to the last segment, often resembling an armored tail or tip of the tail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54e5a979-11d6-4e73-9286-5b7a9738127c",
                                                "sense_id": "273898fe-fc06-3d46-9c54-6911e31df727",
                                                "text": "Although Crangonya evidently comes very close to Niphargus, it appears to be a good genus, and to differ constantly from Niphargus in the more robust body and in the telson, which is always entire and never cleft as in Niphargus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbaca203-958f-427a-8600-31f16a53972d",
                                                "sense_id": "273898fe-fc06-3d46-9c54-6911e31df727",
                                                "text": "The basic number of segments in the abdomen is eleven plus the postsegmental telson which bears the anus, although Matsuda (1976) regards the telson as a twelfth segment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82d28e92-5201-4eac-a5ce-a1adce92c6b9",
                                                "sense_id": "273898fe-fc06-3d46-9c54-6911e31df727",
                                                "text": "The two documented examples of telson abnormalities are on juvenile moults (Fig. 2a, b)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
